# permissions

for windows and macOS users, no need to set any permissions.

## linux

on linux, ditto reads raw keyboard events from `/dev/input/event*` through `evdev`. these files are not readable by regular users by default.

grant the binary read access with:

```sh
sudo setcap cap_dac_read_search=ep "$(which ditto)"
```

ditto still runs as your user, not as root. you will need to run this command again after rebuilding or reinstalling the binary.

to revoke the capability:

```sh
sudo setcap -r "$(which ditto)"
```

